Date:     Wed, 6 Oct 93 11:11:10 GMT
From: starr@genie.slhs.udel.edu
Subject:  My Target Practice

In the true spirit of spontaneous order, I defected from the plans to
co-operate of some Bay Aryan extropians (that didn't seem to be coming
through anyways) and took my .22 pump rifle to the Richmond Rod & Gun
club last Sunday.  A friend who isn't on the list, but has been to
an extropian party or two, came along with his own weaponry.

For $5 admission plus gas & ammo, I got to spend a couple of hours
putting holes in targets 100 yards away.  What fun!  The place wasn't
very crowded at all, but they did require eye and ear protection.  My
friend gave me some disposable earplugs, and I borrowed some goggles
from the club (against policy, but they made an exception for me).  They
also sold ammo cheaper than the gun shop where I got my first box -
only $1.50 for a box of 50 rounds, as opposed to $2.50.  Calibers higher
than .22 were more expensive, but I don't know how they would compare.

My friend's M1 wouldn't fire, possibly due to a broken firing pin, so
we took turns with my rifle, then he got off a few shots with his
revolver before closing.  Interestingly enough, the rest of the hangunners
all had semi-automatics.  There were a couple of guys with .22s with
scopes who were going for real accuracy, and some guys with bigger
rifles whose calibers I didn't make out - but they were loud enough that
I sure was glad for the earplugs!

Turns out my rifle's sight was a bit maladjusted, resulting in groupings
that were a bit to the right and down.  I didn't even manage to hit the
black part of the target, but my friend did - once.  This was even with
the use of a rest on my part.  Of course, the fact that I just found out
I need eyeglasses for long-range vision may have something to do with
my lack of accuracy.  We'll see how I do next time, when we plan on
bringing binoculars so that we can check where we hit after each shot.
Some guys had scopes mounted for the same purpose, independent of their
rifle sights.

All in all, I consumed about 70 rounds, almost a box and a half of ammo.
I can't wait to go back!  Now I want to get a pistol to practice with, too!
And then some archery equipment, throwing knives :-), etc.  Neat stuff!

My friend and I decided we'd like to try to make our outings to the range
sort of monthly, but we haven't decided when we'll go next.  He's got
season tickets for Cal football, so it'll probably have to be another
Sunday.  I'd also like to get out there earlier next time.  We got there
at about 2 p.m., they closed at about 4:15, and that just wasn't enough
time!

So, who's up for coming along next time?  Follow-ups to exi-bay.

